# What the Norwegian constellation names beside this file are, and
# where their claims come from (Sprint 33, issue #347).
#
# The STUDY READS ITS STATUS FROM HERE. It is not a banner the
# generator prints: a report cannot call itself verified because
# somebody edited a string in Java, and it cannot keep calling itself
# provisional after the catalogue has been checked. Status travels
# with the data.
#
# Setting status=verified REQUIRES source, licence, retrieved and
# transformations to be filled in. The generator refuses to run
# otherwise, so "verified" can never be a word without an account
# behind it. Deleting the word PROVISIONAL achieves nothing: the
# report takes its status from this file.
#
# When verification happens, two fields are easy to fill in badly:
#
#   transformations - say "none" explicitly if nothing was changed.
#       Blank stays invalid on purpose. A blank field cannot be told
#       apart from a field nobody got to, and "we changed nothing" is
#       a claim worth making out loud.
#
#   retrieved - an unambiguous ISO date, 2026-09-14, not "September"
#       and not 09/14/26, which means two different days depending on
#       who reads it.
#
#   source - the exact publication or page the names were read from,
#       not the organisation that published it. "Sprakradet" names a
#       body; a reader checking a name needs the document.

status=provisional
rows=88
source=owner-supplied working lead, recorded on issue #347
licence=
retrieved=
transformations=
notes=Crux is given as Sydkorset, the older Dano-Norwegian form; modern Bokmal usage also has Sorkorset. Unresolved until a cited source settles it. The original brightest-star and historical-attribution columns are deliberately excluded.
